# trainer_api: optional OpenVINO export dependencies.
# Installed only when the user opts in via:
#   install_windows.bat --with-openvino
# or manually: `pip install -r requirements-openvino.txt` (the lockfile
# compiled from this manifest; regenerate with
# `uv pip compile requirements-openvino.in -o requirements-openvino.txt --python-version 3.11 --universal`).
#
# Kept separate from requirements.in because the openvino + nncf wheels
# weigh in around 300 MB+ and most users never need IR export. Splitting
# the manifest also makes it easy to audit the OpenVINO license trail
# without scanning the core dependency list.
#
# When adding/upgrading:
#   1. Edit this file.
#   2. Verify the new license is OSS-compatible (Apache-2.0 / MIT / BSD).
#   3. Re-record the LICENSE confirmation URL in the commit body.
#
# License confirmation trail:
#   openvino — Apache-2.0
#     https://github.com/openvinotoolkit/openvino/blob/master/LICENSE
#   nncf     — Apache-2.0 (used for INT8 post-training quantization)
#     https://github.com/openvinotoolkit/nncf/blob/develop/LICENSE

